China is doing much of the heavy lifting for Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> launch, with a 29% sales increase helping offset declines in the U.S. and Japan, according to <a href="https://counterpointresearch.com/en/insights/apple-iphone-18-pro-series-off-to-a-mixed-start-recording-sales-growth-three-weeks-after-launched">Counterpoint Research</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iPhone-18-Pro-Pre-Orders-Feature-Sans-Text.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071763" /><br/>
Combined global sales of the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max rose 3.1% during their first three weeks of availability compared with the equivalent launch period last year. U.S. sales fell 4%, while Japan recorded a 27% decline.<br/>
<br/>
Counterpoint attributed China's growth to better initial supply and higher prices for competing Android flagships. In the U.S., the firm said buyers perceived insufficient changes to features and design, despite additions such as the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/both-iphone-18-pro-models-variable-aperture-camera/">variable aperture camera</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-18-pro-pricing/">raised starting prices</a> by &#36;100 in the U.S., bringing the Pro to &#36;1,199 and the Pro Max to &#36;1,299. Counterpoint pointed out that exchange rates compounded price increases in Japan.<br/>
<br/>
The Pro Max model's share of sales slipped from 57% to 56%, with growth in India and Southeast Asia favoring the smaller model.<br/>
<br/>
